A fiber that has run to its end resumes the context it came from, and
resume() tells AddressSanitizer of the switch, with no place to keep the
fake stack of the context it leaves where that context is done, so that
ASan frees it. It tested the context it switches to instead, which is never
done, and so kept every finished fiber's fake stack: with
detect_stack_use_after_return, ASan's default, each fiber that ends leaves
its fake stack mapped, and a process that makes fibers as it goes grows
without bound. The context left is `from`, and its flag is the one to test.

